-- title:
--   Relative group laws on Weierstrass models over a domain commute
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain, and let $V$ be a projective Weierstrass curve over $R$ whose associated affine Weierstrass equation has invertible discriminant. Write $E = \operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded quotient of the homogeneous coordinate ring of $\mathbb{P}^2_R$ by the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of $V$, equipped with the structure morphism `projModelStrCR V` to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ obtained from `Proj.toSpecZero` followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the map from $R$ into the degree-zero part. Assume `hbc`: for every field $K$ that is an $R$-algebra, the fibre product of `projModelStrCR V` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R \to K$ admits an isomorphism of schemes to `projModelCR (V.baseChange K)`. Let $G$ be a relative group law on `projModelStrCR V`, i.e. operations `mul`, `one`, `inv` on, for each $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, the set of morphisms $\varphi : T \to E$ with $\varphi$ followed by the structure morphism equal to $t$, satisfying associativity, both unit laws, left inverses, and naturality of `mul` under precomposition by any $\psi : T' \to T$ with $\psi$ followed by $t$ equal to $t'$. Then for every scheme $T$, every $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and all such $x, y$ one has $G.\mathrm{mul}\, t\, x\, y = G.\mathrm{mul}\, t\, y\, x$.
--
--   This is the integral-domain case of the commutativity of a group-scheme structure on the smooth proper Weierstrass model $E \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, with no hypothesis relating the unit of $G$ to the section at infinity. It is used further on in the treatment of the relative group law, for instance in establishing reducedness of the kernel scheme attached to a points-evaluation datum.
-- source:
